<http://data.silknow.org/object/6b4457f7-b69a-3301-8e32-a5bcc85ad968/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Wall hanging of embroidered linen canvas with wool and silk in tent and cross stitches. With 17 warps and 14 wefts to the inch. The border of approximately 9 inches wide is filled with grotesque demi-figures, cherubs, animals, birds, plumed masks of lions, fruit and flowers. In the angles of the corners are four panels each containing a word with a symbol: 'VICTVS', 'TECTVM', 'COCORDIA' and 'OPVS'. The central panel has a motif of a group of eight people in rich costume representing a meeting between mounted noblemen and a lady of rank."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6b4457f7-b69a-3301-8e32-a5bcc85ad968> .

